ed $50 million of sales tied to previously written-off or excess inventory obligations.","period_end":"2023-04-30"},{"type":"one_time_dressing","origin":"ai","summary":"The FY2023 Q3 filing reported a $70 million warranty-related benefit in cost of revenue.","period_end":"2022-10-30"},{"type":"one_time_dressing","origin":"ai","summary":"The FY2025 Q1 filing reported a $4.5 billion H20-related charge, while the FY2025 Q2 filing reported $650 million of H20 revenue and a $180 million reserve release.","period_end":"2025-07-27"},{"type":"redefinition","origin":"ai","summary":"The filings changed the presentation of customer concentration from named indirect or direct customers to broader billing-location and headquarters measures.","period_end":"2026-01-25"},{"type":"redefinition","origin":"ai","summary":"The filings changed the scope of purchase commitments from inventory and supply obligations plus other obligations to broader manufacturing, supply, capacity, cloud, investment, and other commitments.","period_end":"2026-01-25"},{"type":"related_party_exposure","origin":"ai","summary":"The filings report substantial share-sale arrangements by directors and executive officers across multiple periods.","period_end":"2026-04-26"},{"type":"subsequent_event","origin":"ai","summary":"The FY2020 Q1 filing reported a planned $7.0 billion Mellanox acquisition that closed immediately after period end.","period_end":"2020-04-26"},{"type":"subsequent_event","origin":"ai","summary":"The FY2022 Q1 filing reported the Arm transaction termination and a $1.35 billion write-off of the signing prepayment.","period_end":"2022-05-01"},{"type":"tagging_quality","origin":"deterministic","summary":"7 XBRL facts were reported at inconsistent scales across filings (e.g. us-gaap:WeightedAverageNumberOfDilutedSharesOutstanding).","period_end":null},{"type":"value_revision","origin":"ai","summary":"The weighted-average diluted-share revisions are substantive share-count restatements rather than clerical formatting changes.","period_end":"2021-05-02"},{"type":"vanishing_item","origin":"ai","summary":"The filings reported an Arm acquisition commitment through FY2021, followed by termination-cost disclosures and no continuing acquisition commitment.","period_end":"2022-05-01"}],"narratives":[{"period_end":"2025-07-27","narrative":"The quarter included approximately $650 million of H20 revenue and a $180 million release of previously reserved H20 inventory. Future commitments included $30.93 billion for fiscal year 2026 and $7.0 billion of expected lease obligations."},{"period_end":"2025-10-26","narrative":"The quarter included $50.3 billion of manufacturing, supply, capacity, and related commitments, plus $26 billion of multi-year cloud commitments. A partner facility-lease guarantee had maximum exposure of $860 million."},{"period_end":"2026-01-25","narrative":"The quarter included $95.2 billion of manufacturing, supply, and capacity commitments and $27 billion of multi-year cloud commitments. The filing also reported $4.0 billion of unrecognized tax benefits and $2.8 billion of product warranty liabilities."},{"period_end":"2026-04-26","narrative":"The quarter included $119 billion of manufacturing, supply, and capacity commitments, with $95 billion payable in the remainder of fiscal year 2027. Partner facility-lease guarantees had maximum gross exposure of $3.5 billion, supported by $712 million of escrow."}],"prose":{"overview":"Revenue reached $252.8 billion over the trailing year, while expenses were $95.0 billion. Revenue grew 67% per year versus 59% for expenses, and total commitments grew 27% per year.","debt":"Total committed money was 1.5x reported debt. The gap reflects $4.3 billion of leases in addition to $8.5 billion of debt.","wall":"The largest payment band is the next five years, with $46.2 billion due. That obligation can be compared with $3.1 billion of deferred revenue and $2.6 billion of backlog already promised to NVIDIA.","flags_note":"The filings show partner facility-lease guarantees with maximum gross exposure of $3.5 billion, supported by $712 million of escrow. They also show presentation changes for customer concentration and purchase commitments, plus substantive weighted-average diluted-share revisions."}}